invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_vector.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: poly1305_vector.h turns the vector Poly1305 on in every file of a host
  object, so poly1305.c under its own names, which a session without
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY runs, multiplies on UMULL, UMLAL or
  PMULUDQ. The tags are the same. test/widemul-builds.sh requires
  poly1305.c in a host object to call neither vector name.

--- old
#if defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE)
--- new
#if defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME)
